<https://chalkline.chelseakr.com/ctdl/resources/ce-58f6b236-9b15-49fa-83c1-eb046ec1ee33>
    a ceterms:License ;
    ceterms:ctid "ce-58f6b236-9b15-49fa-83c1-eb046ec1ee33" ;
    ceterms:description "The Teaching Permit for Statutory Leave (TPSL) allows an employing agency to fill a position where the teacher of record is unable to teach due to a statutory leave (such as a medical leave, Military Leave, or Administrative Leave) with a temporary teacher of record for the duration of the leave.\nHolders of the TPSL are restricted to service with the employing agency requesting the permit. An employing agency is defined as a California public school district, county office of education, nonpublic, nonsectarian school and agency as defined in Education Code sections 56365 and 56366, charter school, or statewide agency. A permit may list multiple LEAs as restrictions. Any LEA may request to be added as an additional restriction on a TPSL permit by submitting an application and half-fee of $50 to the Commission. In this regard, TPSL permit holders may serve across multiple districts.\nThe TPSL may be issued with one or more authorizations in the areas of Multiple Subject, Single Subject, and Special Education, depending on an individual’s qualifications. The permit is renewable upon verification from the employing agency that specific requirements have been completed."@en-us ;
    ceterms:identifier _:c14n1038,
        _:c14n757 ;
