        "Business"@en-us,
        "Dance"@en-us,
        "English"@en-us,
        "For a permit in one of the science subjects, at least nine semester units must be in the specific science area. For a permit in Foundational-Level General Science, an individual has to verify 18 semester units (or nine upper division semester units) across the four science areas of biological science, chemistry, geosciences, and physics. A minimum of one course in each of the four areas is required."@en-us,
        "Foundational-Level General Science"@en-us,
        "Foundational-Level Mathematics"@en-us,
        "Health Science"@en-us,
        "Home Economics"@en-us,
        "Industrial and Technology Education"@en-us,
        "Mathematics"@en-us,
        "Music"@en-us,
        "Note[1]: Individuals who were previously issued an emergency permit in the same subject area of the requested PIP will not be required to submit verification of this requirement. If the subject matter requirement for the emergency permit was met by passage of all appropriate subject matter examinations or degree major, the individual will not qualify for the PIP."@en-us,
        "Physical Education"@en-us,
        "Science: Biological Sciences"@en-us,
        "Science: Chemistry"@en-us,
        "Science: Geosciences"@en-us,
        "Science: Physics"@en-us,
        "Social Science"@en-us,
        "The statutory subjects available for Single Subject Provisional Internship Permit are as follows:"@en-us,
        "Theater"@en-us,
        "World Language: English Language Development"@en-us,
        "World Languages-Languages other than English ( specify )"@en-us ;
    ceterms:name "Single Subject:"@en-us ;
    ceterms:subjectWebpage <https://www.ctc.ca.gov/credentials/leaflets/cl-856/> .

